==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc}} {{term|σῆψις||putrefaction|tr=sēpsis|lang=grc}}, from {{term|σήπειν||to make rotten|tr=sēpein|lang=grc}}, from {{term|σήψ||a kind of lizard, also a kind of serpent whose bite was alleged to cause putrefaction|tr=sēps|lang=grc}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sepses}}

# {{pathology}} A serious medical [[condition]] in which the whole body is inflamed, and a known or suspected infection is present.

